Preserve topology nodes and overlay junctions under GEOS >= 3.15 line merging.

GEOS >= 3.15 returns overlay and unary-union output line-merged
(libgeos/geos#1459), so splits that rtt_AddLine relies on are lost:

- Backport PostGIS commit ca3323d8c748dd806bab188028bb61c5f67b39af
  (https://github.com/postgis/postgis/pull/1160): collect the junctions
  between the shared and non-shared linework of a new line before line
  merging hides them, and re-split the noded line at them.
- librttopo still runs a unary union after splitting the line at existing
  nodes (PostGIS no longer does); split at those nodes again afterwards,
  and do the overlay-junction split after that step.
- Split at the endpoints of the input line that do not lie on linework
  shared with existing edges, so that the start point of a closed input
  line stays a node where it was one with older GEOS.

All extra splits are no-ops with older GEOS.

